# BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile, so this
# list applies to the escoresheet/backend build context without adding a
# .dockerignore inside escoresheet/backend.
#
# An allowlist: only what the server runs from gets into the image. The
# context is the committed tree (build-image.sh, git archive), so an ignored
# file cannot be in it anyway; this list also keeps tests, docs and build
# scripts out, and keeps a dirty test build (--allow-dirty) clean.
*
!server.js
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!lib/
!db/
!scripts/
# never, even inside an allowed directory
**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.dev.vars
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.dump
**/*.sql.gz
**/*.log
